---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

// Roof-week photos: the grid shows resized thumbs (longest side 900px);
// the lightbox opens the full-resolution original via `full`.
const roofWeekPhotos = [
  { src: "/images/roof-week-01-thumb.webp", full: "/images/roof-week-01.webp", alt: "Barn roof torn down to bare decking, with a cupola and rental dumpsters staged on the lawn", w: 675, h: 900 },
  { src: "/images/roof-week-02-thumb.webp", full: "/images/roof-week-02.webp", alt: "Crew working on the barn roof tear-off", w: 900, h: 675 },
  { src: "/images/roof-week-03-thumb.webp", full: "/images/roof-week-03.webp", alt: "Crew continuing to strip the barn roof down to bare decking", w: 900, h: 675 },
  { src: "/images/roof-week-04-thumb.webp", full: "/images/roof-week-04.webp", alt: "The house's gambrel roof mid-tear-off, tarped and exposed near the dormers and chimney", w: 675, h: 900 },
  { src: "/images/roof-week-05-thumb.webp", full: "/images/roof-week-05.webp", alt: "New plywood sheathing installed on the barn roof, with freshly painted siding below", w: 900, h: 675 },
  { src: "/images/roof-week-06-thumb.webp", full: "/images/roof-week-06.webp", alt: "Close-up of the house's gambrel roof mid-tear-off, chimney and dormers exposed", w: 900, h: 675 },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Restoration Progress"
  description="An honest, ongoing record of the restoration of the General Henry Champion House — before, during, and after."
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="relative">
    <img
      src="/images/home-front-spring.webp"
      alt="The General Henry Champion House today, freshly painted with bunting, cannon, and barn visible"
      class="h-[50vh] w-full object-cover"
      width="1920"
      height="1440"
      fetchpriority="high"
      loading="eager"
      decoding="async"
    />
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-black/85 via-black/45 to-black/5"></div>
    <div class="absolute inset-0 flex items-end">
      <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-6xl px-6 pb-12 text-white [text-shadow:0_2px_10px_rgba(0,0,0,0.55)]">
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl">Restoration Progress</h1>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-xl text-lg text-white/90">
          An honest record of the work &mdash; before, during, and after.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16">
    <!-- Origin story -->
    <section id="rescue">
      <h2 class="text-2xl">A House Nearly Lost</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-charcoal)]">
        In January 2024, the Champion House was headed to public auction &mdash; a court-ordered
        foreclosure sale, the end result of years of vacancy and deferred maintenance. The Trust stepped in
        to acquire the property and stop that outcome, taking on a house that had sat empty and
        deteriorating, in order to give it a future instead.
      </p>
      <figure class="mt-6">
        <img
          src="/images/foreclosure-sign-blurred.webp"
          alt="The public auction foreclosure sale sign posted at 526 Westchester Rd, January 2024"
          class="w-full cursor-zoom-in rounded-lg object-cover shadow-sm"
          data-lightbox
          width="1200"
          height="1600"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
        <figcaption class="mt-2 text-xs text-[var(--color-charcoal)]">
          The public auction notice posted at 526 Westchester Rd, January 2024.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <!-- Before condition -->
    <section class="mt-14">
      <h2 class="text-2xl">Where We Started</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-charcoal)]">
        Years of neglect had taken a visible toll: weathered siding, an overgrown lawn and grounds, and a
        roof well past its useful life. These photographs, taken around the time of acquisition, are the
        starting point for everything that's followed.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <img src="/images/restoration-before-siding-thumb.webp" data-full-src="/images/restoration-before-siding.webp" alt="Weathered siding and overgrown grounds at the time of acquisition" class="h-56 w-full cursor-zoom-in rounded-lg object-cover shadow-sm" data-lightbox width="900" height="599" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <img src="/images/restoration-before-aerial-winter.webp" alt="Winter aerial view of the full property, showing the house, pool, and barn" class="h-56 w-full cursor-zoom-in rounded-lg object-cover shadow-sm" data-lightbox width="480" height="360" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <img src="/images/roof-damage-closeup-thumb.webp" data-full-src="/images/roof-damage-closeup.webp" alt="Close-up of the old roof's rotted fascia, exposed rafter tails, and damaged soffit venting" class="h-56 w-full cursor-zoom-in rounded-lg object-cover shadow-sm sm:col-span-2" data-lightbox width="675" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Roof week -->
    <section class="mt-14">
      <h2 class="text-2xl">The Roof Comes First</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-charcoal)]">
        Restoration began where it was needed most urgently: the roof. Water damage doesn't wait, so before
        any cosmetic work could start, both the house and the barn needed new roofs to protect everything
        underneath them.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-charcoal)]">
        Over the weekend of August 1&ndash;2, 2026, a crew tore the old barn roof down to bare decking
        and framed in new plywood sheathing &mdash; while the house's own gambrel roof was stripped to bare
        wood shingles near the dormers and chimney. It was loud, dusty, and genuinely satisfying work to
        watch.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
        {roofWeekPhotos.map((photo) => (
          <img src={photo.src} alt={photo.alt} class="h-40 w-full cursor-zoom-in rounded-lg object-cover shadow-sm" data-lightbox data-full-src={photo.full} width={photo.w} height={photo.h} loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm italic text-[var(--color-charcoal)]">
        More photos of the completed roof work coming soon.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Today -->
    <section id="today" class="mt-14">
      <h2 class="text-2xl">The House Today</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-charcoal)]">
        With new roofs installed on both the house and barn, the property is already looking more like
        itself. There's more work ahead, including finishing touches on the roofs themselves, but the
        hardest, most urgent phase is behind us.
      </p>
      <img
        src="/images/home-front-overcast.webp"
        alt="The house today, front elevation with patriotic bunting and cannon on the lawn"
        class="mt-6 h-96 w-full cursor-zoom-in rounded-lg object-cover shadow-sm"
        data-lightbox
        width="1024"
        height="1024"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <section class="mt-16 rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-stone)] bg-[var(--color-parchment)] px-8 py-10 text-center">
      <h2 class="text-2xl">More to Come</h2>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-xl leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-charcoal)]">
        This page will grow as the work continues &mdash; new photos, new phases, and an honest look at
        what it takes to bring a 1790 landmark back.
      </p>
      <a href="/donate" class="btn-primary mt-6 shadow-lg shadow-black/50 ring-1 ring-white/15">Support the Restoration</a>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>
